  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates which lottery has the lower probability of loss and prefers that one. Here, Lottery A has 0% chance of loss, Lottery B has 1%, so the reason would prefer A. However, the individual chooses B *because* the loss probability in B is small — not because it is lower than in A (which it is not), but despite A being safer. The individual’s reasoning downplays the existence of a loss in B and uses it to justify choosing B, but does not compare loss probabilities to select the lower one. In fact, they choose the lottery with the higher probability of loss. Thus, while the individual considers the probability of loss, they do not apply the rule of the decision reason (minimize probability of loss). Instead, they use the small size of the risk to justify risk-taking, which is a different logic. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the prescribed way.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
}

